<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>All the news about Africa - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:10:14 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Africa</category><title>French ambassador to CAR disciplined over misconduct allegations</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260812-french-ambassador-to-car-disciplined-over-misconduct-allegations</link><description>
France’s foreign ministry has launched disciplinary proceedings against its ambassador to the Central African Republic, following allegations that he repeatedly brought young women to the official residence in Bangui and had sexual relations with some of them.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/051412da-9634-11f1-8957-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/french-ambassador-bangui.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/051412da-9634-11f1-8957-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/french-ambassador-bangui.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38edf5ea-9624-11f1-aab5-b1eab2020edd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:02:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/051412da-9634-11f1-8957-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/french-ambassador-bangui.jpeg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Race to find Ebola vaccine as DR Congo outbreak kills more than 2,000</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260812-race-to-find-ebola-vaccine-as-dr-congo-outbreak-kills-more-than-2-000</link><description>
The latest outbreak of Ebola has killed more than 2,000 people in the Democratic Republic of Congo, according to health authorities. Meanwhile, international efforts have been stepped up to test a vaccine for the highly contagious haemorrhagic fever.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/50759716-959a-11f1-af1b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223437161951.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/50759716-959a-11f1-af1b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223437161951.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7534c1c2-962f-11f1-b43d-f3a546cf71d4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:44:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/50759716-959a-11f1-af1b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223437161951.jpg">AP Photo/Dieudonne Dirole - Dieudonne Dirole</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rebel forces in Ethiopia's Tigray state condemn army drone strikes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260811-rebel-forces-in-ethiopia-s-tigray-state-condemn-army-drone-strikes</link><description>
Rebel authorities on Tuesday accused the Ethiopian government of carrying out deadly drone strikes in southern Tigray state and condemned the move as "a serious escalation", amid fears of a new war. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de06147a-1d45-11f1-a5b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-afp-march-2026-000-A26B6PM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de06147a-1d45-11f1-a5b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-afp-march-2026-000-A26B6PM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b05c8bea-9567-11f1-8107-913aa69e7026</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 13:25:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de06147a-1d45-11f1-a5b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-afp-march-2026-000-A26B6PM.jpg">AFP - ABEL GEREZGIHER</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ghana backs Jamaica's petition to push UK for slavery reparations</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260810-monday-o-n-ghana-backs-jamaica-s-petition-to-push-uk-for-slavery-reparations</link><description>
Jamaica and Ghana, both former British colonies subjected to the transatlantic slave trade, are presenting a united front in the drive for reparatory justice. As Kingston prepares to lodge a formal petition with King Charles III seeking to advance its claim for reparations from the United Kingdom, Ghana's president says the global movement to address the legacy of slavery has reached a "defining moment". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e3557ba8-28d9-11ef-adee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_326P2UC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e3557ba8-28d9-11ef-adee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_326P2UC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66eb257c-91aa-11f1-aa99-717baab8f235</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:01:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e3557ba8-28d9-11ef-adee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_326P2UC.jpg">AFP - RICARDO MAKYN</source><dc:creator>Zeenat Hansrod</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Investigation raises alarm over uranium in DRC cobalt shipments to China</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260809-investigation-raises-alarm-over-uranium-in-drc-cobalt-shipments-to-china</link><description>
An investigation by Lighthouse Reports, The Financial Times and Le Monde traces the possible export of uranium from the Democratic Republic of Congo back to a confidential International Atomic Energy Agency memo obtained in 2024. Chinese mining group CMOC, which owns the main site examined in Katanga, disputes the findings.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8bc47d66-cce7-11ed-8528-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32MK4U2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8bc47d66-cce7-11ed-8528-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32MK4U2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a89e4b5e-90a9-11f1-aa9f-076e9a7b708c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 10:53:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8bc47d66-cce7-11ed-8528-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32MK4U2.jpg">© AFP/Junior Kannah</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ivorian drum, looted by France, goes on display for first time at home</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260808-ivorian-drum-looted-by-france-goes-on-display-for-first-time-djidji-ayokwe</link><description>
The Djidji Ayokwe, a sacred "talking drum" which was looted by French colonial troops in 1916 and taken to France, arrived in its home village in Côte d'Ivoire on Friday, where local people were able to see it for the first time since it was repatriated in March. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bc3fc75c-381e-11f1-acc7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98CW9TK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bc3fc75c-381e-11f1-acc7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98CW9TK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5410b5fe-9315-11f1-83b6-5f422980672c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 10:52:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bc3fc75c-381e-11f1-acc7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98CW9TK.jpg">AFP - BERTRAND GUAY</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DR Congo hands first prisoners back to M23 rebels under peace deal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260807-dr-congo-hands-first-prisoners-back-to-m23-rebels-under-peace-deal</link><description>
In a long-awaited operation, Democratic Republic of Congo authorities released 15 prisoners and handed them over to rebels from the AFC/M23 movement on Friday. It marks the first known prisoner transfer under a peace deal signed last year to end fighting in the eastern DRC.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bf38ab10-7557-11f1-8fb2-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3C393L.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bf38ab10-7557-11f1-8fb2-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3C393L.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">95284640-924a-11f1-bbad-41bd60add3e8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 18:17:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bf38ab10-7557-11f1-8fb2-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3C393L.jpg">AFP - JOSPIN MWISHA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ex-Benin president Talon makes political comeback via newly founded Senate</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260807-ex-benin-president-talon-makes-political-comeback-via-newly-founded-senate</link><description>
Benin’s newly created Senate elected former president Patrice Talon as its leader on Thursday in Porto-Novo, less than three months after he left office. He will serve a five-year term at the head of the country’s new second chamber of Parliament.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0d1ec63e-9213-11f1-8b41-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-30T193143Z-1836495194-RC2BOMAX7QRY-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0d1ec63e-9213-11f1-8b41-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-30T193143Z-1836495194-RC2BOMAX7QRY-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">896400f2-9235-11f1-8846-ada1b72c7d88</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 11:47:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0d1ec63e-9213-11f1-8b41-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-30T193143Z-1836495194-RC2BOMAX7QRY-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-POLITICS.jpg">REUTERS - Charles Placide Tossou</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ceuta and Western Sahara at heart of US-Morocco rapprochement</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260806-ceuta-and-western-sahara-at-heart-of-united-states-morocco-rapprochement</link><description>
Since late July, the United States has been increasingly signalling a move to strengthen its ties with Morocco, both economically and diplomatically. In 2020, the US backed Morocco’s autonomy plan for Western Sahara in exchange for the country normalising relations with Israel. Now, Washington appears ready to support Morocco’s claims regarding the Spanish enclaves of Ceuta and Melilla. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/427a96a8-90e9-11f1-a773-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-05T135156Z-302699241-RC2NPMAFOLSZ-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/427a96a8-90e9-11f1-a773-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-05T135156Z-302699241-RC2NPMAFOLSZ-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ce5abc4-9181-11f1-91c0-09d83fba7db7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:22:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/427a96a8-90e9-11f1-a773-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-05T135156Z-302699241-RC2NPMAFOLSZ-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg">REUTERS - Violeta Santos Moura</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ebola cases near 4,000 as DRC struggles to contain fast-spreading outbreak</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260806-ebola-cases-near-4-000-as-drc-struggles-to-contain-fast-spreading-outbreak</link><description>
The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic ⁠of Congo is spreading faster than efforts to fight it, the head of the World Health Organization has warned, with nearly 4,000 confirmed cases so far. With five provinces known to be affected, authorities in Kinshasa are concerned about the deadly virus reaching the capital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f4c5e8-9170-11f1-9699-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/drc-ebola-healthworkers-afp-000-C24F84F.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f4c5e8-9170-11f1-9699-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/drc-ebola-healthworkers-afp-000-C24F84F.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ea4eb92-916e-11f1-a12e-c965799e264c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 11:25:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f4c5e8-9170-11f1-9699-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/drc-ebola-healthworkers-afp-000-C24F84F.jpg">© AFP - BENEDICTION MURHABAZI </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigeria approves $4.5bn refinancing of state-owned oil company</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260805-nigeria-approves-4-5bn-refinancing-of-state-owned-oil-company</link><description>
Nigeria has approved a new $4.5 billion loan to replace a 2023 loan of $3.3 billion. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/745a2774-75fa-11f1-ab00-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26082376854419.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/745a2774-75fa-11f1-ab00-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26082376854419.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8de7b16e-9000-11f1-a59b-7542df06581f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 12:20:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/745a2774-75fa-11f1-ab00-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26082376854419.jpg">AP - Sunday Alamba</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ugandan military honours Netanyahu’s brother with Entebbe memorial statue</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260804-ugandan-military-honours-netanyahu-s-brother-with-entebbe-memorial-statue</link><description>
Uganda’s military has unveiled a monument to Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s older brother, who was killed during a hostage rescue operation in the East African country in 1976.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5b2a8386-8fe8-11f1-b226-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/A-monument-honoring-the-late-Yoni-Netanyahu-AP26215390559044.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5b2a8386-8fe8-11f1-b226-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/A-monument-honoring-the-late-Yoni-Netanyahu-AP26215390559044.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c87aca9c-8feb-11f1-9bba-1346dae39c0f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 15:29:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5b2a8386-8fe8-11f1-b226-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/A-monument-honoring-the-late-Yoni-Netanyahu-AP26215390559044.jpg">Uganda Peoples' Defence Forces P - Uganda Peoples' Defence Forces P</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ghana bets on AI and coding in bid to modernise national curriculum</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260804-ghana-bets-on-ai-and-coding-to-modernise-basic-education-africa-technology</link><description>
Ghana has introduced artificial intelligence, coding and computer programming into its national curriculum, for pupils from kindergarten to junior high school, becoming one of the few African countries to embed these subjects in basic education.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4eebdc2-8cc4-11f1-a382-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Picture-3-7.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4eebdc2-8cc4-11f1-a382-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Picture-3-7.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dc6d6782-8cc4-11f1-b4ed-dd19f77b313a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 09:01:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4eebdc2-8cc4-11f1-a382-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Picture-3-7.jpeg">© Michael Sarpong Mfum</source><dc:creator>Michael Sarpong Mfum in Ghana</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Cameroon government says Biya's prolonged absence 'no cause for concern'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260803-cameroon-government-says-president-biya-s-prolonged-absence-no-cause-for-concern</link><description>
President Paul Biya left Cameroon in early June for what his office described as a "short private stay in Europe". Addressing concerns over this prolonged absence, a government spokesperson told RFI the 93-year-old head of state is healthy and hard at work. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/46322daa-8ef1-11f1-92ec-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7X96PA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/46322daa-8ef1-11f1-92ec-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7X96PA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43f082b6-8f29-11f1-a565-b12c1aa1cb82</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:58:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/46322daa-8ef1-11f1-92ec-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7X96PA.jpg">AFP - ALBERTO PIZZOLI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Benin’s new Senate raises questions over power and legitimacy</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260803-benin-s-new-senate-raises-questions-over-power-and-legitimacy</link><description>
Benin’s new senate was inaugurated in Porto-Novo last week, creating a second chamber of parliament with powers to review legislation, protect constitutional rules and discipline political figures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fcfc79a8-d44a-11f0-b461-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-12-08T110950Z-9433312-RC29CIAHRLSM-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-SECURITY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fcfc79a8-d44a-11f0-b461-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-12-08T110950Z-9433312-RC29CIAHRLSM-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-SECURITY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a265bb6-8bf5-11f1-a2cf-377d54a72fad</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:32:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fcfc79a8-d44a-11f0-b461-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-12-08T110950Z-9433312-RC29CIAHRLSM-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-SECURITY.jpg">REUTERS - Charles Placide Tossou</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Hundreds flee Ethiopia to war-torn Sudan, following new fighting in Tigray</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260803-hundreds-flee-ethiopia-to-war-torn-sudan-following-new-fighting-in-tigray</link><description>
In Ethiopia, hundreds of people have fled to Sudan following Saturday's fighting, when clashes in Tigray pitted federal forces against rebels from the Tigray People's Liberation Front. Both sides accuse the other of seeking to trigger a new conflict. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a6327e60-8f20-11f1-a0a4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-2026-afp-000-A26B6PB.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a6327e60-8f20-11f1-a0a4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-2026-afp-000-A26B6PB.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b34f8102-8f1f-11f1-90aa-db88ccb4d9a8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:01:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a6327e60-8f20-11f1-a0a4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-2026-afp-000-A26B6PB.jpg">AFP - ABEL GEREZGIHER</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Sudan army's drone attack on court building kills 35 in Darfur, NGO says</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260803-sudan-army-s-drone-attack-on-court-kills-35-in-darfur-ngo</link><description>
A Sudanese rights group reported that the Sudanese army struck a traditional court in a Rapid Support Forces-held village in North Darfur with drones on Sunday, killing 35 people.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/556b7ef0-374b-11f1-9147-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-824J2WE-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/556b7ef0-374b-11f1-9147-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-824J2WE-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e8adaec-8f19-11f1-97a7-458f4247222d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 09:56:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/556b7ef0-374b-11f1-9147-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-824J2WE-1.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>'Marriage is no longer a shield': new law in Mauritius recognises marital rape</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260802-marriage-is-no-longer-a-shield-new-law-in-mauritius-recognises-marital-rape</link><description>
Mauritius's parliament has unanimously voted to criminalise marital rape and impose harsher sentences for femicide, after a spate of violent attacks against women exposed serious gaps in protection. New reforms aim to improve safeguards for victims who have long gone unheard and unprotected.
